---
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="Mark Lee writes Learning Loons from Singapore.">
  <article class="article">
    <header>
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>I’m Mark Lee.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I write this site. There is no editorial team hiding behind the loon.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Learning Loons used to introduce itself as a lifelong-learning brand for “fun learning
        facts and educational shorts,” with a tagline that ran <em>life long learningand
        Bite-Sized Learning</em> into itself. That was the WordPress theme talking. I am a
        writer in Singapore. I publish essays here, and I keep a short shelf of tools I have
        actually built.
      </p>
      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        A reading room. Newer pieces tend to be long: death and TV, hoarding, money, faith,
        sobriety, teens, confinement, the tuition industry. Older study-skill notes are still
        here if they help someone, but they are not the front of the house.
      </p>
      <h2>What I will cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How people learn — memory, language, school, AI as a tutor rather than a personality.</li>
        <li>Parenting and Singapore classrooms, including ADHD and autism, without turning them into SEO tags.</li>
        <li>Mind and meaning: the series on wanting it all, sharing, scarcity, giving up.</li>
        <li>Small builds that already live off this site (Telegram, Firebase), described honestly.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What I will not cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A kids’ fact mill, or a promise of daily educational shorts. Video is a separate problem.</li>
        <li>A SkillsFuture course catalogue. The word showed up in the old meta description. It is not the job of this site.</li>
        <li>Comments, membership, or a shop. There were none worth keeping.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. That is the address on the
        legal pages. I am the same person who ships Issued, Ms. Lee, Cassy Care, Gains Guardian,
        and WhereBabe.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
